  "question": {
    "text": "Three lines are drawn from the origin $O$ with direction cosines proportional to (1,-1,1) (2,-3,0) and $(1,0,3) .$ The three lines are"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "not coplanar",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "coplanar",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "perpendicular to each other",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "coincident",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\quad$ $\\Delta=\\left|\\begin{array}{ccc}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right|$\r\n$=1(-9-0)-(-1) \\cdot(6-0)+1(0-(-3))$\r\n$=-9+6+3=0$\r\nsince, $\\Delta=0$\r\n$\\therefore$ Lines are coplanar."
  }
}